  m_text: "This is the central pediment tympanon block of the front fa\xE7ade. It
    bears sculptural decoration with a male bust in a wreath  in the center, held
    by two flying Victories. The male figure bears the cone-capped quiver and the
    bow, iconographic features of Apollo, a god  whom Emperor Caracalla appealed
    to for healing, and who appears in coinage minted during the same period. Contrary
    to this pediment, the back pediment was constructed by multiple blocks and was
    left blank."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
